.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:379:          "rationale": "Withheld pending the macOS credential transport decision, not because the entitlement is unusable. Two distinct facts. (a) The .spec/security-privacy.md design — secrets in the DATA PROTECTION Keychain shared host-to-provider through one access group — cannot work here, because that keychain is available only to code running in a user context and access groups share items between programs running as the same user, while this provider runs as root. (b) The entitlement itself IS grantable to a root system extension and is used in production: PureVPN's packet-tunnel system extensions carry keychain-access-groups, and Surfshark's instead carries a temporary-exception path for /Library/Keychains/, both pointing at the FILE-BASED System keychain rather than the Data Protection Keychain. Which of those the provider needs is exactly what TASK-260728-7ii1xz decides, so under least privilege the row stays withheld until a transport is selected rather than provisioning a right whose purpose is undetermined.",
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json-380-          "evidence": "Observed 2026-07-28 on this Mac via codesign -d --entitlements :- on the installed system extensions.",
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json-381-          "resolutionOwner": "TASK-260728-7ii1xz",
